@startuml "Flux de requête utilisateur"

title Flux de requête utilisateur classique

participant "Load Balancer\n(HAProxy)" as LB
participant "Frontend\n(Next.js)" as Frontend
participant "API Gateway\n(Next.js API)" as API
participant "Rate Limiter\n(Redis)" as RateLimit
participant "Auth Service\n(JWT + Sessions)" as Auth
participant "Business Services" as Services
participant "Cache Layer\n(Redis)" as Cache
participant "Database\n(PostgreSQL)" as DB
participant "Monitoring\n(Prometheus)" as Monitoring
participant "Logging\n(Winston)" as Logging

User -> LB: HTTPS Request
LB -> LB: SSL Termination
LB -> Frontend: Forward to available instance

Frontend -> Frontend: Server-side rendering (SSR)
Frontend -> API: Internal API call
API -> RateLimit: Check rate limits
RateLimit -> Cache: GET rate_limit:{user_id}
Cache --> RateLimit: current count
RateLimit -> RateLimit: Increment counter

alt Rate limit OK
    RateLimit --> API: Request allowed
    API -> Auth: Authenticate request
    Auth -> Cache: GET session:{token}
    Cache --> Auth: session data
    
    alt Valid session
        Auth --> API: User authenticated
        API -> Services: Business logic
        Services -> Cache: GET cached_data:{key}
        Cache --> Services: cached result
        
        alt Cache miss
            Services -> DB: Query database
            DB --> Services: data
            Services -> Cache: SET cached_data:{key} = data (TTL)
        end
        
        Services --> API: Response data
        API -> Monitoring: Record metrics
        API -> Logging: Log request
        API --> Frontend: JSON response
        Frontend --> LB: HTML response
        LB --> User: HTTPS Response
        
    else Invalid session
        Auth --> API: 401 Unauthorized
        API --> Frontend: Redirect to login
        Frontend --> LB: Redirect response
        LB --> User: Redirect to login
    end
    
else Rate limit exceeded
    RateLimit --> API: 429 Too Many Requests
    API --> Frontend: Rate limit error
    Frontend --> LB: Error response
    LB --> User: Rate limit response
end

@enduml